+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support handled a high
+volume of tickets but closed a smaller share of them than the team's own
+dashboard reported. Security maintained a strong incident resolution rate.
+The delivery plan is on track, with the launch landing in late October once
+all four phases (Discovery, Build, QA, Release) are accounted for.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+Three figures in the source packets do not match their own underlying data
+and should be corrected at the source before wider distribution:
+
+- **Finance:** the packet's stated total spend ($463,250) is $750 lower than
+  the sum of its own itemized categories ($464,000, from payroll +
+  infrastructure + contractors + facilities). The itemized sum was used
+  above; the surplus figure reflects it.
+- **Support:** the packet's stated close rate (96.4%) does not match its own
+  ticket counts. 1,171 closed of 1,250 opened is 93.7%, not 96.4%. This is a
+  meaningful gap and worth confirming with the support team before it's
+  cited externally.
+- **Delivery:** the packet's stated launch date (2026-10-22) corresponds to
+  the end of the QA phase, not the end of the Release phase. Adding the
+  1-day Release phase (accounting for the 2026-10-12 company holiday and
+  weekends) puts the actual launch date at 2026-10-23. The plan itself looks
+  healthy; the packet's summary line just needs correcting.
+
+Security's incident resolution rate (95.0%, 76 of 80 resolved) checks out
+against the underlying counts and needs no action.
